foundation.question_text:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown. Sketch $y=-f(x)$, marking the image of the point $(1,2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.3,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-0.5:4.2,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-3*\x*\x+4.5*\x});
\node[blue,right] at (3.4,3.0) {$y=f(x)$};
\fill (1,2) circle (2pt) node[above] {$(1,2)$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$(3,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
$y=-f(x)$ reflects across the $x$-axis: $(x,y)\to(x,-y)$.
$(1,2)\to(1,-2)$, and $(3,0)$ stays on the $x$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.3,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-0.5:4.2,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-3*\x*\x+4.5*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-0.5:4.2,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-(0.5*\x*\x*\x-3*\x*\x+4.5*\x)});
\node[gray,right] at (3.3,2.9) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue,right] at (3.3,-2.9) {$y=-f(x)$};
\fill[gray] (1,2) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (1,-2) circle (2pt) node[below] {$(1,-2)$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$(3,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

