mastery.question_text:
The dashed curve is $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the solid curve is $y=(x+1)^{2}$. Name the reflection and justify it with function notation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-3.0,0)--(3.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.7)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-0.73:2.73,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.73:0.73,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x+1)*(\x+1)});
\node[gray,right] at (1.7,2.7) {$y=(x-1)^{2}$};
\node[blue,left] at (-1.7,2.7) {$y=(x+1)^{2}$};
\fill[gray] (1,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$(1,0)$};
\fill (-1,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$(-1,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
